                Question(prompt: "When some bones are missing, how do scientists complete a skeleton?",
                         options: ["Making up random bones", "Using plastic toys", "They give up", "Comparing with similar dinosaurs"], correctIndex: 3,
                         explanation: "It is rare to find every single bone of a dinosaur. When some are missing, scientists compare the skeleton with close relatives to work out the right shape. Sometimes they make careful copies of the missing bones so the skeleton can stand complete in a museum."),
                Question(prompt: "What is the science of studying ancient life through fossils called?",
                         options: ["Paleontology", "Astronomy", "Geography", "Cooking"], correctIndex: 0,
                         explanation: "Paleontology is the science of studying ancient life using fossils. Paleontologists explore rocks all over the world, searching for clues about dinosaurs, ancient plants, and other creatures. It blends detective work, science, and a great deal of patience and curiosity."),
                Question(prompt: "Which dinosaur was the very first to be given a scientific name?",
